  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Can you imagine living all day in a cave without a smartphone? In southwest France, a team of 15 volunteers did just this for up to 40 days!"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The group was sent to a cave with no phone, clock, water, or light. The volunteers had to use a special bike to produce electricity. They drew water from a well that was 45 metres underground. Since the group didn’t have clocks, they soon lost all sense of time. They did things like eating and sleeping according to their body clocks."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "This experiment was part of a project called “Deep Time”. The idea behind it was to test how people would "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "respond",
      "ref": "v-respond"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to losing their sense of time. The volunteers’ brain activity was examined before and after the experiment. Some scientists had been observing the volunteers during their time in the cave."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "After they left the cave, some volunteers said they wanted to stay there for a while longer. “"
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "Away from",
      "ref": "v-away-from"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the busy city life, we could stop to live our lives peacefully,” said one volunteer."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
